#DESCRIPTION
Ion Beam-Beam Instability Standalone Test - HYBRID PIC
(kinetic ions / massless fluid electrons)

Hybrid counterpart of PARAM.in (the full-PIC beam test).  The electrons are
replaced by an implicit massless neutralizing fluid, so the plasma is a single
kinetic ion species (H+) and the ion beam-beam instability is driven purely by
the kinetic-ion two-stream / cyclotron response.  The grid, guide field, beam
ratio/speeds, density, normalization and output are identical to PARAM.in so the
FFT transverse-wave validation applies unchanged.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-1e3                    xMin
 1e3                    xMax
-1.0                    yMin
 1.0                    yMax
-1.0                    zMin
 1.0                    zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall term drives the ion-scale electromagnetic beam-beam instability.
#HALLTERM
T                       useHallTerm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass        Species 0: H+
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: H+ (quasi-neutral)
-0.4                    ux [km/s normalized; -400 km/s background]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.0e-9                  bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

TESTCASE Beam splits the single H+ species: 1% of the macroparticles become the
beam (ux = +0.4, weight scaled up), the remaining 99% the colder background
(weight scaled down), preserving total particle count and mass.  The mean Vx is
conserved at 0.01*0.4 + 0.99*(-0.4) = -0.392.
#TESTCASE
Beam
0                       iSpecies
0.01                    ratio
0.4                     vel
0.0                     vel
0.0                     vel

Digital-filter smoothing of the ion moments before the Ohm's law low-passes the
PIC shot noise whose time-integration by Faraday produces spurious transverse
field drift, while conserving the domain mean so the beam-beam instability seed
is preserved.
#SMOOTHMOMENTS
T                       doSmoothMoments
1                       nSmoothMoments
0.5                     coefSmoothMoments

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.001                   dt

#NORMALIZATION
1000.0                  lNormSI
1.0e6                   uNormSI

#MONITOR
10                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii planet  plotString
-1                      dn
0.02                    dt
1                       dx
rhoS0 Bx By Bz          varName

#PARTICLETRACKER
T           usePT

#TPPARTICLES
4           particles per cell in X
4           particles per cell in Y
1           particles per cell in Z

#TPREGION
uniform         region

#TPCELLINTERVAL
64          nIntervalX
1           nIntervalY
1           nIntervalZ

#TPSAVE
0           iSpecies
planet      IOUnit
10          dnSave
0.5         launchThreshold

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
0.1                     TimeMax

#RUN
